KG42.register("edges-916a9c75f057d9a0344c64ad",{"id":"S-1383f44b8239a02a","source":"COMP-aa22fdcebf0da947","type":"links","target":"COMP-3e92318d3f30d9b2","evidence_class":"S","scientific_acceptance":false,"relation_scope":"original_occurrence_pair_only","internal_to_parent":false,"paper_ids":["01-central_pool"],"assertions":[{"id":"01-central_pool::v141-c-R007::E::v141-c-R007-E001","paper":"01-central_pool","rule_id":"v141-c-R007","rule_ref":"01-central_pool::v141-c-R007","record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R007-E001","source":"coordination.local_operator","target":"settlement.payment","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R007-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e001"]},"evidence_class":"S","provenance_gate":"direct_C_edge_with_constraint_and_source_excerpt","scientific_acceptance":false,"accepted_constraint_ids":["v141-c-R007-C001"],"held_constraint_ids":[],"semantic_review_status":"supported","source":"COMP-aa22fdcebf0da947","target":"COMP-3e92318d3f30d9b2","source_occurrence_id":"01-central_pool::v141-c-R007::V::coordination.local_operator","target_occurrence_id":"01-central_pool::v141-c-R007::V::settlement.payment","source_unit_id":"01-central_pool::v141-a-M01::coordination.local_operator","target_unit_id":"01-central_pool::v141-a-M01::settlement.payment","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"settlement","context_text":"Aggregate monetary flows for internal community energy exchanges. | Community peak-power penalty remunerating the DSO for public-grid capacity. | External-grid energy payments of entities belonging to the community. | Redistribution of community revenues and costs among all member entities by the upper-level community operator. | Valuation of each entity's internal community energy exchanges at each time period in its energy revenues-and-costs account.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e001","v141-b-g01-e009","v141-b-g02-E15","v141-b-g02-E16","v141-b-g02-E30","v141-b-g04-E12"]},"active":true,"source_signature":"9b19babb4a6916913d00efb431a6b1c9fa87341e381c06c52772a21e8a9fe82e","relation_scope":"original_occurrence_pair_only","internal_to_parent":false,"source_science":{"mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","source_definition":"A common operator has lower dispatch coordination, contracts, fee remuneration and upper non-deterioration benefit-sharing roles; retain role branches.","target_definition":"A source composite of entity marginal valuation, operator fees, external tariffs/taxes and non-deterioration redistribution; not one settlement equation.","constraints":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R007-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The community microgrid operator redistributes revenues and costs among the members subject to the non-penalization condition. Scope: Redistribution of community revenues and costs among all member entities by the upper-level community operator. Condition: Each member's outcome within the community must be no worse than its outcome when acting individually.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator","settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e001","v141-b-g01-e012","v141-b-g01-e013","v141-b-g02-E03"]}],"evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e001","location":{"location_id":"src-13c261d954-p01-c2r2__v141-a-M01-participation","page":1,"printed_page":null,"section":"Abstract","anchor_text":"T lettib, Antonio Giannitrapanib, Italy ext of community microgrids, where members of a community ca","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-01.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"A market-oriented pricing of energy exchanges within the community is obtained by implementing an internal local market based on the marginal pricing scheme. The market aims at maximizing the social welfare of the community, thanks to the more efficient allocation of resources, the reduction of the peak power to be paid, and the increased amount of reserve, achieved at an aggregate level. A community microgrid operator, acting as a benevolent planner, redistributes revenues and costs among the members, in such a way that the solution achieved by each member within the community is not worse than the solution it would achieve by acting individually. In this way, each member is incentivized to participate in the community on a voluntary basis. The overall framework is formulated in the form of a bilevel model, where the lower level problem clears the market, while the upper level problem plays the role of the community microgrid operator."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e012","location":{"location_id":"src-13c261d954-p05-c1r1__v141-a-M01-participation","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.1. The bilevel model","anchor_text":"B. Cornélusse, et al. the executed quantities, ad • the community prices, • the community symmetric ","equation_id":"(3)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"Then, the role of the upper level is to share among the entities the profits of the community, by ensuring that no entity is penalized with respect to acting individually. Indeed, a community is composed of several entities driven by self-interests. In order to achieve a long-lasting community microgrid, each entity should be stimulated to participate in the community on a voluntary basis. This is achieved by enforcing the condition\n$J_u \\geq J_u^{SU} \\quad \\forall u \\in \\mathcal{U},$  (3)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e013","location":{"location_id":"src-13c261d954-p05-c1r2__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.1. The bilevel model","anchor_text":"y y y g g condition eu Ju JuSU u , (3) where JuSU is the optimal profit of entity u when acting indi","equation_id":"(3)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"where $J_u^{SU}$ is the optimal profit of entity u when acting individually, while $J_u$ is the profit of entity u within the community. As a consequence, the upper level can be seen as a benevolent planner, that manages the community microgrid in the best interest of all the participants. If at least one inequality in (3) is satisfied strictly, the state of the community is termed Pareto superior to the state when entities act individually [23]."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E03","location":{"location_id":"src-13c261d954-p05-c1r1__v141-a-M01-participation","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.1","anchor_text":"B. Cornélusse, et al. the executed quantities, ad • the community prices, • the community symmetric ","equation_id":"(3)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"In order to achieve a long-lasting community microgrid, each entity should be stimulated to participate in the community on a voluntary basis. This is achieved by enforcing the condition J_u >= J_u^SU, ∀u ∈ U, (3) where J_u^SU is the optimal profit of entity u when acting individually, while J_u is the profit of entity u within the community. As a consequence, the upper level can be seen as a benevolent planner, that manages the community microgrid in the best interest of all the participants. If at least one inequality in (3) is satisfied strictly, the state of the community is termed Pareto superior to the state when entities act individually [23]."}],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"settlement","context_text":"Aggregate monetary flows for internal community energy exchanges. | Community peak-power penalty remunerating the DSO for public-grid capacity. | External-grid energy payments of entities belonging to the community. | Redistribution of community revenues and costs among all member entities by the upper-level community operator. | Valuation of each entity's internal community energy exchanges at each time period in its energy revenues-and-costs account.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e001","v141-b-g01-e009","v141-b-g02-E15","v141-b-g02-E16","v141-b-g02-E30","v141-b-g04-E12"]},"source_record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R007-E001","source":"coordination.local_operator","target":"settlement.payment","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R007-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e001"]},"paper_scope_note":"Operational responsibilities, lower-level clearing output, energy valuation, fees, and upper-level sharing are kept separate; the price equation retains import/export and complementary slackness conditions. The ordering of the two-level LP is limited only to the unique-solution and cascaded-solution branches."}}],"assertion_ids":["01-central_pool::v141-c-R007::E::v141-c-R007-E001"]});
